## ArXiv Mining

ArXiv lists every paper author by name — and many link directly to their institution page, LinkedIn, or personal site.

**How to use it:**

1. Go to [arxiv.org](https://arxiv.org) → search by topic (e.g. `LLM inference`, `RLHF`, `transformer efficiency`)
2. Filter by date — last 6–12 months for active researchers
3. Click author names → follow co-author networks
4. Cross-reference on Google: `"First Last" site:linkedin.com`

**High-signal topics to search:**
- `vLLM`, `Flash Attention`, `LoRA`, `quantization`, `speculative decoding`
- `RLHF`, `Constitutional AI`, `reward modeling`
- `MLSys`, `model serving`, `inference optimization`
- `ASIC`, `neural network accelerator`, `silicon photonics`

**Tools:** [Semantic Scholar](https://www.semanticscholar.org) · [Papers With Code](https://paperswithcode.com) · [Connected Papers](https://www.connectedpapers.com)

